{"availability":"available","full":"IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari","name":"tavily-hikari","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":362,"forks":53,"created":"2025-10-31T09:01:50Z","updated":"2026-10-07T14:33:49Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ivanli-cn.github.io/tavily-hikari/","topics":["search"],"demo":"https://ivanli-cn.github.io/tavily-hikari/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.449Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.449Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.449Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:03.271Z","stars":362,"forks":53},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.449Z","stars":362,"forks":53}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[]( []( [](rust-toolchain.toml) [](web/package.json) []( [](README.zh-CN.md)","Tavily Hikari is a Rust + Axum proxy for Tavily's MCP endpoint. It multiplexes multiple API keys, anonymizes upstream traffic, stores full audit logs in SQLite, and ships with a React + Vite web console for realtime visibility.","Looking for the Chinese documentation? Check README.zh-CN.md."],"features":["Key pool with fairness – SQLite keeps last-used timestamps and assigns each access token a short‑lived “home” key; new or expired affinities are resolved via least‑recently‑used selection across active keys to keep wear…","Short IDs and secret isolation – every Tavily key receives a 4-char nanoid. The real token is only retrievable via admin APIs/UI.","Health-aware routing – status code 432 automatically marks keys as exhausted until the next UTC month or manual recovery.","Segmented reconciliation for anonymized billing – when accessToken mode is active and both rebalance switches are enabled, Hikari records real (token, key, period) usage, actively closes Research in bounded background…","Full audit trail – requestlogs persists method/path/query, upstream responses, error payloads, and the list of forwarded/dropped headers."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f8bea0054dc8a5003ac485e6ffa820cc33276ebd7e2431019d9637881b2f4181","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:03.433Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.593Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"[]( []( [](rust-toolchain.toml) [](web/package.json) []( [](README.zh-CN.md)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Split PWA identities – the public/user web app installs from /, /console, /login, and /registration-paused, while the admin web app installs only from /admin/; both can reopen their shell offline, but live data and mutations stay network-only.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It serves the normal Public, User Console, Admin, Login, and Registration Paused pages while VITEDEMOMODE=true intercepts /api/ and /mcp inside the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"First Linux DO login automatically creates and binds one Hikari access token.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f8bea0054dc8a5003ac485e6ffa820cc33276ebd7e2431019d9637881b2f4181","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.594Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T14:33:49Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IvanLi-CN/tavily-hikari/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:44.596Z","hash":"f8bea0054dc8a5003ac485e6ffa820cc33276ebd7e2431019d9637881b2f4181","originalBytes":36064,"storedBytes":36064,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["admin","linuxdo","tavily","api","hikari","key","token","user","auth","bun","credit","